1
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:12,281
Rule 207: Inventory Management — scope of the chapter

2
00:00:12,281 --> 00:00:17,966
Yaad rakho: Basic rules sabke liye, detail department ki, par Chapter 7 ke hisaab se

3
00:00:17,966 --> 00:00:30,757
Scope: Ye rule poore chapter ka "scope clause" hai — isme koi sub-rule, clause ya proviso nahi hai. Ye batata hai ki Chapter 7 ke basic rules kis par lagte hain aur departmental instructions ki kya hadd hai.

4
00:00:30,757 --> 00:00:49,047
Rule 207: Do baatein: (1) is chapter ke basic rules sab Ministries/Departments par lagte hain; (2) koi bhi Ministry/Department apne detailed instructions aur procedures bana sakta hai — lekin woh "broadly in conformity" hone chahiye, yaani Chapter 7 ke basic rules ke khilaf nahi ja sakte.

5
00:00:49,047 --> 00:01:02,600
Exam trap: Kya koi department Chapter 7 se hat kar apne inventory rules bana sakta hai? Nahi. Detailed instructions "broadly in conformity" with Chapter 7 hone chahiye — conformity test Rule 207 ka core hai.

6
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:07,190
Rule 208: Receipt of goods and materials from private suppliers

7
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:12,270
Yaad rakho: C.I.R.T.S. — Contract, Inspect, Record, Technical check, Stock register

8
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:24,442
Receipt: Rule 208 mein sirf ek sub-rule hai — Rule 208(1) — jiske andar teen clauses (i), (ii), (iii) hain. Ye tab lagta hai jab maal bahar ke private supplier se aata hai (internal division se aane par Rule 209 lagega).

9
00:01:24,442 --> 00:01:31,756
Rule 208(1): Heading clause. Iske niche (i) se (iii) teen mandatory steps hain — contract dekho, verify karo, register karo.

10
00:01:31,756 --> 00:01:48,226
Clause (i): Sabse pehla kadam contract terms padhna hai. Delivery schedule, specification, inspection clause, packaging, insurance — jo kuch contract mein likha hai, receipt usi ke hisaab se honi chahiye. Contract ke bina receipt matlab aage chalkar dispute mein department kamzor padega.

11
00:01:48,226 --> 00:02:04,417
Clause (ii): Teen physical cheezein har baar honi chahiye: counting, measuring ya weighing, aur visual inspection — aur ye sab receipt ke time par hi. Visual inspection ke teen objective hain: quantity sahi hai, quality specification ke hisaab se hai, aur koi damage/deficiency nahi.

12
00:02:04,417 --> 00:02:09,609
Note: Rule 208 mein koi footnote ya proviso nahi hai — poora rule teen clauses ka hai.

13
00:02:09,609 --> 00:02:18,872
Exam trap: Technical inspection kab karwani hogi? "Where required" — jahan zaroori ho, approved Technical Inspector ya approved Agency se. Har baar nahi.

14
00:02:19,442 --> 00:02:25,527
Rule 209: Receipt / issue of goods and materials from internal divisions of the same organisation

15
00:02:25,527 --> 00:02:30,407
Yaad rakho: Indent, Examine, Acknowledge, (na mile to) entry in indentor copy

16
00:02:30,407 --> 00:02:46,079
Issue: Rule 209 mein chaar clauses hain: (i) internal division se maal mangwana, (ii) stock se maal dena, (iii) contractor ko diye gaye maal ki recovery acknowledgement, aur (iv) poora indent pura na kar sakein to kya karna hai — ye last clause sabse zyada ignore hota hai.

17
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:59,111
Clause (i): Maal mangwane wala officer (indenting officer) prescribed form mein indent dega. Maal milne par woh khud examine/count/measure/weigh karega — quantity, quality, damage — teen check Rule 208(ii) jaisi hi hain.

18
00:02:59,111 --> 00:03:16,161
Clause (ii): Stock se maal nikalne ka rule: Officer-in-charge ensure karega ki prescribed form ka indent pehle hi maujood hai. Uske baad maal issue karte waqt likhit ya online acknowledgement lena hoga — indenting officer ya uske authorised representative se, aur woh bhi issue ke time par.

19
00:03:16,161 --> 00:03:24,026
Note: Rule 209 ke (i) mein receipt SHALL hai jabki Rule 208(iii) mein supplier ko receipt dena MAY hai — ye contrast yaad rakhiye.

20
00:03:24,026 --> 00:03:35,264
Exam trap: Contractor ko diya gaya maal — acknowledgement mein kya likhwana zaroori hai? Sirf receipt nahi — recovery rates aur total value chargeable, contractor se signed aur dated.

21
00:03:35,834 --> 00:03:39,046
Rule 210: Custody of goods and materials

22
00:03:39,046 --> 00:03:44,224
Yaad rakho: Safe custody + Storage + Temperature + Dust-free = Rule 210

23
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:58,711
Custody: Rule 210 ek single-paragraph rule hai — koi sub-rule ya clause nahi. Chhota par bhaari: yahi rule storage ki physical responsibility tay karta hai, aur isi ke na-manne se aksar Rules 33–38 ke loss cases bante hain.

24
00:03:58,711 --> 00:04:15,492
Rule 210: Jis officer ke paas samaan ki custody hai, woh chaar cheezein ensure karega: (1) safe custody — security, lock, access control; (2) proper storage accommodation — jagah, racks, handling; (3) required temperature; (4) dust-free environment.

25
00:04:15,492 --> 00:04:22,834
Note: Rule 210 mein "etc." hai — matlab temperature aur dust-free minimum examples hain, poori list nahi.

26
00:04:22,834 --> 00:04:32,144
Exam trap: Rule 210 kis par zyada sakht hai? "Especially valuable and/or combustible articles" par — dono category high-risk hain.

27
00:04:32,714 --> 00:04:35,184
Rule 211: Lists and Accounts

28
00:04:35,184 --> 00:04:40,390
Yaad rakho: Actual balance = Book balance, kisi bhi waqt check ho sake

29
00:04:40,390 --> 00:04:52,539
Accounts: Rule 211 do sub-rules aur ek Note mein hai. (i) general requirement — item-wise lists/accounts; (ii) chaar alag-alag registers; Note — forms mein aur detail jodi ja sakti hai.

30
00:04:52,539 --> 00:05:05,555
Clause (i): Do duties: item-wise lists + accounts rakhna, aur accurate returns banana. Asal test ye hai: kisi bhi waqt asal balance (physical) aur book balance (register) ki tulna ho sake.

31
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:11,763
Clause (ii): Chaar category ke liye alag-alag accounts — ek hi register sab kuch nahi.

32
00:05:11,763 --> 00:05:27,382
Note: Departments in forms mein aur columns jod sakte hain (jaise warranty expiry, AMC details, location code). Par jo GFR likhta hai, wahan se hatna nahi — minimum to hona hi chahiye — supplement karna hai, replace karna nahi.

33
00:05:27,382 --> 00:05:42,464
Exam trap: Kaunsa form kis asset ke liye? GFR-22 Register of Fixed Assets · GFR-23 Stock Register of consumables · GFR-18 Accession Register (library books) · GFR-24 Register of assets of historical/artistic value.

34
00:05:43,034 --> 00:05:46,048
Rule 212: Hiring out of Fixed Assets

35
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:51,005
Yaad rakho: Record + Regular recovery + Historical cost = Rule 212

36
00:05:51,005 --> 00:05:58,574
Accounts: Rule 212 bhi ek single paragraph hai — teen requirements: record, regular recovery, historical cost basis.

37
00:05:58,574 --> 00:06:34,544
Rule 212: Jab koi fixed asset (jaise departmental genset, machinery, vehicle, tentage) kisi local body, contractor ya kisi aur ko kiraye par diya jaaye, to teen cheezein: (1) asset ka proper record — kaunse asset, kisko, kab se kab tak; (2) hire aur dusre charges regularly recover karne honge — charges wahi jo competent authority ke prescribed rules ke under hain; (3) charges ki ganana historical cost par hogi — matlab asset jis price par kharida gaya tha (uski original cost), aaj ke market rate ya replacement cost par nahi.

38
00:06:34,544 --> 00:06:46,132
Note: Rule 212 khud koi rate prescribe nahi karta — rates "rules prescribed by the competent authority" se aate hain. Rule sirf basis (historical cost) fix karta hai.

39
00:06:46,132 --> 00:06:55,304
Exam trap: Hire charges kis par based honge? Historical cost par — market rate, replacement cost ya insurance value par nahi.

40
00:06:55,874 --> 00:07:01,031
Rule 213: Physical verification of Fixed Assets and Consumables

41
00:07:01,031 --> 00:07:07,836
Yaad rakho: Ek saal, Dono category, Custodian saamne, Certificate, Discrepancy, R.33–38

42
00:07:07,836 --> 00:07:20,800
Verification: Rule 213 teen sub-rules ka hai: 213(1) fixed assets, 213(2) consumables, 213(3) verification ka procedure (teen clauses). Isi rule se verification ki poori kahani chalti hai.

43
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:40,282
Rule 213(1): Teen baatein: (a) fixed assets ka inventory ordinarily site par rahega — matlab jahan asset hai wahin record bhi, alag jagah file mein nahi; (b) verification kam se kam saal mein ek baar; (c) verification ka nateeja corresponding register mein darj ho.

44
00:07:40,282 --> 00:07:53,318
Rule 213(2): Consumables ka bhi wahi frequency — saal mein kam se kam ek baar — lekin nateeja stock register mein darj hoga, aur wahan se aage competent authority action legi.

45
00:07:53,318 --> 00:08:06,927
Note: Rule 213(3)(iii) Chapter 7 ko Chapter 2 ke "Defalcation and losses" (Rules 33–38) se jodta hai — shortage ka matlab automatic penalty nahi, balki reporting chain shuru hona hai.

46
00:08:06,927 --> 00:08:16,712
Exam trap: Fixed assets aur consumables — dono ki verification frequency? Dono "at least once in a year" (213(1) aur 213(2)).

47
00:08:17,282 --> 00:08:19,213
Rule 214: Buffer Stock

48
00:08:19,213 --> 00:08:24,383
Yaad rakho: Buffer = authority tay kare, 1 saal se upar = generally surplus

49
00:08:24,383 --> 00:08:33,788
Planning: Rule 214 ek chhota rule hai par iska Note poore chapter ka sabse cited line hai — "ek saal se zyada stock mein pada material generally surplus".

50
00:08:33,788 --> 00:08:52,660
Rule 214: Optimum buffer stock competent authority tay karega — ye koi fixed number nahi jo GFR mein likha ho. Tay karte waqt teen factors dekhne honge: requirement ki frequency, quantity, aur supply ka pattern (lead time, reliability). Matlab buffer stock ek analysis ka nateeja hai, guess nahi.

51
00:08:52,660 --> 00:09:05,055
Note: Ye note do kaam karta hai. Pehla: reasoning — inventory carrying cost aisa kharch hai jo material ki value nahi badhata, isliye bina wajah stock rakhna financial propriety ke khilaf hai.

52
00:09:05,055 --> 00:09:16,160
Exam trap: Buffer stock ka optimum level kaun tay karta hai? Competent authority — frequency, quantity aur supply pattern ke base par. GFR koi fixed figure nahi deta.

53
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:20,609
Rule 215: Physical verification of Library books

54
00:09:20,609 --> 00:09:26,529
Yaad rakho: 20,000 = har saal, 50,000 = 3 saal, usse upar = sample, 5 per 1,000

55
00:09:26,529 --> 00:09:37,961
Verification: Rule 215 library books ke liye Rule 213 ka special exception hai — yahan do clauses hain: (i) verification ka scale-based schedule, (ii) reasonable loss ka norm.

56
00:09:37,961 --> 00:09:55,245
Clause (i): Teen slabs: ≤ 20,000 volumes → har saal complete verification; 20,000 se zyada aur 50,000 tak → kam se kam 3 saal mein ek baar complete verification; 50,000 se zyada → sample verification, jinke beech ka interval 3 saal se zyada na ho.

57
00:09:55,245 --> 00:10:10,828
Clause (ii): Pehla hissa ek concession hai: ek saal mein jitni books issue/consult hui unmein har 1,000 par 5 volumes ki loss reasonable maani ja sakti hai — par sirf tab jab woh dishonesty ya negligence ki wajah se na ho.

58
00:10:10,828 --> 00:10:23,280
Note: Rule 215, Rule 213 ke "at least once in a year" se exception hai — library books par scale-based schedule lagta hai, annual nahi (siwaye ≤20,000 volumes wale library ke).

59
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:31,640
Exam trap: 30,000 volumes wale library mein verification? Complete verification kam se kam 3 saal mein ek baar.

60
00:10:32,210 --> 00:10:36,165
Rule 216: Transfer of charge of goods, materials etc.

61
00:10:36,165 --> 00:10:40,566
Yaad rakho: Statement, Dono sign with date, Dono ke paas copy

62
00:10:40,566 --> 00:10:48,985
Accountability: Rule 216 ek paragraph ka rule hai — lekin yahi tay karta hai ki charge badalne ke baad kisi bhi kami ki zimmedari kiski hogi.

63
00:10:48,985 --> 00:11:14,881
Rule 216: Teen requirements: (1) jaane wala (transferred) officer ensure karega ki goods/materials sahi tareeke se successor ko hand over ho jayen — sirf chabi dena kaafi nahi; (2) ek statement banega jismein goods/materials ki saari relevant details hon, aur use relieving (charge lene wale) aur relieved (charge chhodne wale) dono officers date ke saath sign karenge; (3) dono ek-ek copy rakhenge.

64
00:11:14,881 --> 00:11:22,472
Note: Rule 216 mein koi proviso ya exception nahi — ye har transfer par lagta hai, chahe charge kitne din ka ho.

65
00:11:22,472 --> 00:11:30,392
Exam trap: Statement kaun sign karega? Relieving aur relieved — dono, date ke saath. Sirf ek ka sign kaafi nahi.

66
00:11:30,962 --> 00:11:33,237
Rule 217: Disposal of Goods

67
00:11:33,237 --> 00:11:38,863
Yaad rakho: Declare, Record reasons, Value, GFR-10, Responsibility, E-waste rules

68
00:11:38,863 --> 00:11:47,965
Disposal: Rule 217 paanch clauses ka hai aur poore disposal process ka pehla darwaza hai. Iske bina Rule 218 ka koi mode choose nahi kiya ja sakta.

69
00:11:47,965 --> 00:12:04,714
Clause (i): Declaration tab ho sakti hai jab item Ministry/Department ke kaam ka na rahe. Par declaration kaun karega — woh authority jo item kharidne ke liye competent hai (authority competent to purchase). Aur us authority ko reasons record karne hi honge.

70
00:12:04,714 --> 00:12:22,412
Clause (ii): Committee banana vivek-adhikar hai — "may, at his discretion". Matlab committee zaroori nahi, par bade ya sensitive lots ke liye banana behtar practice (aur aksar departmental instructions mein likha hota hai). Exam mein ye MAY vs SHALL ka favourite sawal hai.

71
00:12:22,412 --> 00:12:37,013
Clause (iii): Teen prices nikalne honge: book value, guiding price, reserved price. Agar book value nikalna sambhav na ho, to original purchase price use kiya ja sakta hai (yahan "may be utilised" ek permitted fallback hai).

72
00:12:37,013 --> 00:12:46,178
Clause (iv): Agar item kisi Government servant ki negligence, fraud ya mischief se unserviceable hua ho, to responsibility fix karni hogi.

73
00:12:46,178 --> 00:12:57,632
Note: Rule 217(v) GFR ko E-Waste (Management) Rules, 2022 aur MoEF&CC guidelines se jodta hai — isliye Special Campaign mein e-waste disposal ka alag se target hota hai.

74
00:12:58,202 --> 00:13:00,650
Rule 218: Modes of Disposal

75
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:06,090
Yaad rakho: ₹4 lakh = Tender ya Auction, ₹2 lakh = 10 July 2024 se pehle

76
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:16,495
Disposal: Rule 218 chaar clauses ka hai aur amended hai: clause (i) ki threshold DoE OM F.1/3/2024-PPD (10 July 2024) se ₹2 lakh se badhkar ₹4 lakh ho gayi.

77
00:13:16,495 --> 00:13:36,080
Clause (i): Assessed residual value (na ki original purchase value) ₹4,00,000 se upar ho to disposal sirf do tareeqon se: (a) advertised tender se bids, ya (b) public auction. DONO mein se koi ek chunna hai — teesra raasta (direct sale, quotation, committee decision) allowed nahi.

78
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:54,441
Clause (ii): ₹4 lakh se kam residual value par mode competent authority tay karegi, lekin bina reason ke nahi — teen objectives dhyan mein rakhne honge: (1) samaan ka jama hona rokna, (2) jagah block na hona, (3) disposal hone wale samaan ki value kharab na hona.

79
00:13:54,441 --> 00:14:14,706
Clause (iii): Kuch cheezein bechi nahi ja sakti — expired medicines, food grain, ammunition jaise hazardous ya human consumption ke layak na hone wale items ko turant dispose ya destroy karna hai, suitable mode se. Teen wajah: health hazard, environmental pollution, aur misuse ki sambhavna.

80
00:14:14,706 --> 00:14:25,304
Note: Clause (i) aur (ii) dono mein threshold ek hi hai aur dono amendment ke saath badalte hain — 10 July 2024 se pehle dono jagah ₹2 lakh tha.

81
00:14:25,874 --> 00:14:29,300
Rule 219: Disposal through Advertised Tender

82
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:34,924
Yaad rakho: 9 steps (a)–(i), 7 aspects (a)–(g), 10% bid security, late bid = no

83
00:14:34,924 --> 00:14:43,844
Sale: Rule 219 teen hisson mein hai: (i) nau broad steps (a) se (i), (ii) saat important aspects (a) se (g), aur (iii) late bids ka rule.

84
00:14:43,844 --> 00:15:01,491
Clause (i): Nau kadam: bidding document banana → tender invite karna → bids kholna → analysis/evaluation → highest responsive bidder chunna → sale value collect karna → sale release order dena → goods release karna → unsuccessful bidders ki bid security wapas karna.

85
00:15:01,491 --> 00:15:22,176
Clause (ii)(a): Chaar value: transparency, competition, fairness, discretion ka khatma. Sale plan aur goods ka wide publicity zaroori. Saari terms bidding document mein comprehensive, plain and simple language mein honi chahiye — chhupe hue conditions nahi. Aur taxes ka applicability document mein saaf likha ho.

86
00:15:22,176 --> 00:15:38,077
Clause (ii)(b): Bidding document mein goods ka location aur present condition dono likhne honge, taaki bidder bidding se pehle inspect kar sake. Isse "jo dekha wo mila" wala dispute nahi hota — isliye condition chhupana rule ke khilaf hai.

87
00:15:38,077 --> 00:15:46,545
Note: (i) mein nau steps hain (a)–(i), jabki (ii) mein saat aspects (a)–(g) — dono ki numbering alag hai, confuse na karein.

88
00:15:46,545 --> 00:15:54,632
Exam trap: Bid security kitni? Ordinarily assessed ya reserved price ka 10% — exact amount bidding document mein.

89
00:15:55,202 --> 00:15:57,826
Rule 220: Disposal through Auction

90
00:15:57,826 --> 00:16:02,526
Yaad rakho: 25% spot earnest money, Cash ya DACR, IFW officer zaroori

91
00:16:02,526 --> 00:16:14,122
Sale: Rule 220 paanch clauses ka hai: (i) kaun karayega, (ii) principles + publicity, (iii) auction shuru mein dobara ghoshna, (iv) hammer stroke + earnest money, (v) team mein IFW officer.

92
00:16:14,122 --> 00:16:27,915
Clause (i): Auction do tareeqe se ho sakti hai: khud (directly) ya approved auctioneers ke through. Dono valid hain — "approved auctioneers" ka matlab hai ki kisi bhi private auctioneer ko nahi, approved ko hi lena hai.

93
00:16:27,915 --> 00:16:45,615
Clause (ii): Principles wahi — transparency, competition, fairness, discretion ka khatma. Auction plan mein goods ki details, unka location aur sale ki terms hon, aur use utni hi wide publicity mile jitni advertised tender ko milti hai. Matlab chupke se auction karwana allowed nahi.

94
00:16:45,615 --> 00:17:01,361
Clause (iii): Auction shuru karte waqt ek baar phir ghoshit karein: goods ki condition, location, aur terms & conditions — ikathhe hue bidders ke faayde ke liye. Publicity mein likha hua phir se bolna zaroori hai, taaki koi bole "mujhe pata nahi tha".

95
00:17:01,361 --> 00:17:08,807
Note: 25% earnest money aur 10% bid security (Rule 219) mein farq yaad rakhiye — auction mein 25%, tender mein 10%.

96
00:17:08,807 --> 00:17:16,400
Exam trap: Auction mein earnest money kitni? Bid value ka kam se kam 25% — turant, mauke par, cash ya DACR mein.

97
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:20,928
Rule 221: Disposal at scrap value or by other modes

98
00:17:20,928 --> 00:17:27,064
Yaad rakho: Tender fail, Auction fail, Scrap (CA + Finance), Eco-friendly destruction

99
00:17:27,064 --> 00:17:37,884
Sale: Rule 221 ek paragraph ka hai, par iski pre-condition sabse important hai — ye tabhi lagta hai jab advertised tender aur auction dono try karke dekh liye hon.

100
00:17:37,884 --> 00:17:58,533
Rule 221: Do stages. Stage 1: agar advertised tender ya auction ke bawajood item nahi bikta, to scrap value par becha ja sakta hai — par competent authority ki approval ke saath Finance division se consultation karke. Yani do alag cheezein: approval (competent authority) + consultation (Finance division).

101
00:17:58,533 --> 00:18:04,999
Note: Rule 221 "MAY" hai — lekin condition ke saath: pehle dono sale modes try karne honge.

102
00:18:04,999 --> 00:18:17,600
Exam trap: Kya bina tender/auction try kiye seedha scrap value par bech sakte hain? Nahi. "In spite of its attempts through advertised tender or auction" — pehle dono try zaroori.

103
00:18:18,170 --> 00:18:20,226
Rule 222: Sale Account

104
00:18:20,226 --> 00:18:25,133
Yaad rakho: Form GFR-11, Sale supervise karne wale officer ke sign

105
00:18:25,133 --> 00:18:33,620
Records: Rule 222 ek line ka rule hai — disposal ke baad ka antim record. Chhota par audit mein sabse pehle yahi maanga jaata hai.

106
00:18:33,620 --> 00:18:52,983
Rule 222: Dispose kiye gaye goods ka sale account Form GFR-11 mein banega, aur us par us officer ke sign honge jisne sale ya auction ki supervision ki. Dhyan dein: sign karne wala wohi officer hai jisne supervise kiya — koi aur officer "on behalf" sign nahi kar sakta is rule ke under.

107
00:18:52,983 --> 00:18:59,084
Note: Rule 222 kisi bhi mode ke baad lagta hai — tender ho, auction ho ya scrap sale.

108
00:18:59,084 --> 00:19:05,912
Exam trap: Sale account kaun sign karta hai? Woh officer jisne sale/auction supervise kiya.

109
00:19:06,482 --> 00:19:08,901
Rule 223: Write-off of losses

110
00:19:08,901 --> 00:19:14,631
Yaad rakho: Sanction har haal mein, 4 depreciation heads, 5 non-depreciation heads

111
00:19:14,631 --> 00:19:24,563
Write-off: Rule 223 teen sub-rules mein hai: (1) powers to write off, (2) depreciation wale losses ke 4 heads, (3) depreciation ke alawa wale losses ke 5 heads.

112
00:19:24,563 --> 00:19:43,917
Rule 223(1): Teen baatein: (1) revaluation, stock-taking ya kisi aur wajah se hone wale profit aur loss dono record kiye jayenge aur zaroorat padne par adjust kiye jayenge; (2) formal sanction competent authority ki leni hogi — chahe government accounts mein koi correction/adjustment ho ya na ho.

113
00:19:43,917 --> 00:20:00,470
Rule 223(2): Depreciation se hone wale loss ko chaar heads mein baant kar record karna hai: (i) market price ka normal utaar-chadhav; (ii) normal ghisavat (wear & tear); (iii) kharid regulate karne mein foresight ki kami; (iv) kharid ke baad negligence.

114
00:20:00,470 --> 00:20:18,742
Rule 223(3): Depreciation ke alawa wale losses ke paanch heads: (i) chori ya fraud; (ii) upeksha (neglect); (iii) obsolescence ya zarurat se zyada kharid ki anticipated losses; (iv) damage (nuksan); (v) Force Majeure — aag, baadh, dushman ki action jaise extraordinary situations.

115
00:20:18,742 --> 00:20:28,228
Note: Rule 223(1) ka "even though no formal correction or adjustment in government accounts is involved" — sabse zyada poocha jaane wala line.

116
00:20:28,228 --> 00:20:41,864
Exam trap: Accounts mein koi adjustment nahi hoga to bhi sanction chahiye? Haan — Rule 223(1) clear roop se kehta hai "even though no formal correction or adjustment in government accounts is involved".

